      "repair_reason": "- [P2] The remaining action is maintainer merge judgment around SDK fallback compatibility and current-head proof, not an automated repair.; Cleared: No security or supply-chain regression was found; the diff only changes a shared response-reading helper and focused tests. (sha=3bb967d115070c24bf56a888b1cf55dd0a3ba439)",
      "review_summary": "The PR changes `readResponseText` so capped reads without a readable stream fail closed before whole-body fallbacks, and adds regression tests for capped fallback avoidance, native bodyless responses, and uncapped UTF-8 byte accounting.\n\nPR surface: Source +10, Tests +44. Total +54 across 2 files.\n\nReproducibility: yes. Source inspection of current main and the latest release shows capped `readResponseText` calls without a readable stream can fall through to whole-body `arrayBuffer()` or `text()` fallbacks.",
